## 3. Motions and animations

Animations should make OmniLens feel responsive, not slow or distracting.

Button interactions

Short, subtle hover, pressed and focus transitions. Buttons should respond immediately to clicks.

Card interactions

Subtle elevation or movement on hover, without making the layout jump or shift.

Loading and processing

Lightweight loading indicators with clear status text. Stop the animation as soon as processing finishes or is cancelled.

Live detection

Update bounding boxes smoothly using fresh detections. Avoid flashy scanning animations, delayed box transitions or animations that make objects appear in the wrong position.

Accessible motion

Respect the operating system's reduced-motion preference. Never make animations the only way to communicate status.

## 4. Clickables and interaction correctness

This is one of the most important improvements. Every visible interactive element must perform its advertised action.

| Element                        | Expected behaviour                                                               |
| ------------------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Feature card                   | Opens the correct feature when the card itself is intended to be clickable       |
| Start camera                   | Requests permission and starts the camera                                        |
| Stop camera                    | Stops the camera and releases its media tracks                                   |
| Microphone button              | Starts or stops voice input and visibly indicates listening state                |
| Find Object                    | Accepts the target and searches actual camera frames                             |
| Read Text                      | Runs OCR on the captured image and displays or speaks the actual recognised text |
| Describe Surroundings          | Analyses the current image and provides a grounded description                   |
| Stop Speech                    | Immediately stops current speech playback                                        |
| Repeat Speech                  | Repeats the latest available result                                              |
| Sensitivity slider             | Updates the actual detector configuration, not just the displayed number         |
| Flip Photo / Invert Directions | Applies the intended setting independently                                       |
| Navigation links               | Open the correct page and show which section is active                           |
| Retry button                   | Retries the failed operation instead of merely dismissing the error              |

Also fix accidental double-clicks, dead buttons, nested clickable conflicts, controls that look enabled when unavailable, and controls that trigger the wrong action.

## 5. Correctness of the four feature interfaces

Live Detection

